# Response headers for the static site. Cloudflare reads this file from the build output
# and does not serve it as a page.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# Every page:
#   X-Content-Type-Options  a browser must not guess a file's type from its contents
#   Referrer-Policy         a link out says which site it came from, never which page
#   X-Frame-Options         no other site may show these pages inside a frame
#   Permissions-Policy      the site uses none of these, so no script on it may ask
#
# There is deliberately no Content-Security-Policy. /admin loads its editor from unpkg
# and talks to GitHub, and the pages carry small inline scripts; a policy that is wrong
# by one source breaks publishing or the size picker, and nothing would report it. It
# needs its own piece of work, tested against /admin with a real sign-in.
#
# /_astro/: everything Astro emits there has a hash of its contents in its name — CSS,
# scripts, optimised images, fonts — so a changed file is a new address and the old one
# can be kept for a year. Without this each of them is re-checked on every visit.

/*
	X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
	Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
	X-Frame-Options: DENY
	Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

/_astro/*
	Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
